# sync.yaml — a FORK's declaration of its parent (pull-based sync, the git fork model).
#
# The template itself carries NO sync.yaml: it is a ROOT repo — `bun sync:check` on it
# prints "root repo, nothing to check" and exits 0. A fork copies this file to its repo
# root as `sync.yaml`, fills it in, and inherits the whole tool for free.
#
# USER DECISION (2026-07-21): "o template não sabe dos filhos; os filhos declaram o pai."
# The parent never lists its children. Reverse flow (a fix born in a fork that belongs in
# the parent) is always an explicit PR to the parent — never automation.
#
# The contract has exactly THREE keys (scripts/sync/contract.ts is the typed source):
#
#   parent     — { repo, ref }: where you forked from, pinned to a FULL commit sha.
#                A branch name is a moving target, not a pin; sync:pull rewrites the sha.
#   inherited  — path globs that MUST byte-match the parent at the pinned ref.
#                sync:check fails per file on ANY divergence: modified content, a missing
#                inherited file, or a child-only file that appeared under these globs.
#                Fix menu: (a) re-pull · (b) reclassify to adapted WITH a why · (c) upstream a PR.
#   adapted    — exact files (never globs) that came from the parent and DELIBERATELY
#                diverged. Each entry carries a mandatory `why`. Liveness-gated: the file
#                must exist in the child AND differ from the parent at the pin — an adapted
#                file that matches the parent again is a fossil and fails the gate.
#
# Everything NOT declared here is OWNED by the child; the tool never touches it.
# Never list sync.yaml itself under `inherited` — it is the child's own declaration.
#
# Commands (shipped by the parent, inherited by every fork):
#   bun sync:check              CI drift gate — exit 1 on any drift or dead adapted entry
#   bun sync:pull [--to <ref>]  apply the parent's surface changes, advance the pin
#   SYNC_PARENT_PATH=<path>     use a local clone of the parent (offline / tests)

parent:
  repo: git@github.com:acme/template-fullstack.git
  ref: 4f1c9b2e7d3a5c8f0b6e1d4a9c2f7b3e8d5a0c1e # full 40-char sha — advance with `bun sync:pull`

inherited:
  - scripts/** # the tooling itself rides the train — including scripts/sync/**
  - packages/api/typescript/core/**
  - packages/api/go/core/**
  - .claude/skills/**

adapted:
  - path: docs/BACKEND.md
    why: rewritten around this product's bounded contexts; upstream shape no longer fits
  - path: packages/api/typescript/core/src/config/defaults.ts
    why: product-specific defaults (quota tiers) — upstreaming would leak product vocabulary
